WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:04.036
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test--

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:07.807
the steel sheet stab
and brass rod chop.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.174
To test the strength
of your tips,

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.876
as well as all your edges,
I'm going to be stabbing

00:00:10.976 --> 00:00:12.178
and chopping at these targets.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.445
Remember, this test
is all about what

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:15.114
these targets do to
your daggers and not

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.982
what your daggers do to them.

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:17.817
Dorian, you're up first.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:18.751
You ready?

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.653
 You break it, you buy it.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:21.688
 I don't have that much money.

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.796
[clang]

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:34.633
 Well, Dorian, it
looks like your blade

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.571
got Superman punched right
after the ring of the bell, man.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.240
However, that doesn't mean that
you're out of this competition.

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:43.109
Jarrod, Jimmy,
both of your blades

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.245
have to survive at least one
strike against our test media

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:48.247
in order for you to move
forward in this competition.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.215
If one of you fails
on the first strike,

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.984
then we move into
a deliberation.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.853
So there's still
a chance, Dorian.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:54.820
Good luck, gentlemen.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:55.555
Ben.

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:04.064
 [exhales]

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.899
 Well, Jarrod, you survived.

00:01:06.965 --> 00:01:08.434
Your blade here is substantial.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:08.968
Nice job.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.135
 Thank you.

00:01:10.202 --> 00:01:11.704
 Jimmy, you ready for this?

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.472
 Yes, sir.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.217
[exhales]

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.888
 Well, Jimmy, your tip
held up beautifully.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.457
I can't even tell that it
went through a piece of steel.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.524
Nice job.

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:33.726
It's really a testament
to the heat treat

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.460
you did on this blade here.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.195
 OK.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.935
 Dorian, unfortunately,
your blade suffered

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.136
a catastrophic failure.

00:01:44.236 --> 00:01:46.038
You cannot move
forward with testing.

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:48.108
I'd like to invite you
to shake our hands,

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.776
shake your competitors' hands,
and then exit the forge.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:53.146
Come on forward, my friend.

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:53.912
Good job, Dorian.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.280
 Thank you, sir.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.049 line:0%
I'm definitely bummed
that all my work just kind

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:58.084 line:7%
of went down the drain.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:58.885
 Thanks for all the hard work.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.119
 It was an honor.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:01.487
I knew I had a soft
spot in my blade.

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:03.556
You know, I did rush
the heat treat process.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.258
When you have that
clock going, there's

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.226
those little details that
will come back and bite you.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:09.262
And that's what happened
today during testing.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.336
 Jarrod, Jimmy,
congratulations.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.572
You guys have made it to
the third and final round

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:20.673
of this competition.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.675
Now it's time to shake
it down to your bones,

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:25.545
as we send you back to your home
forges to make one of these--

00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:36.288
the horseman's tabar
with a hidden dagger.

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.223
 I've never had to make
anything with something

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.725
hidden in the handle before.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.929
So I have no idea how I'm
going to put this together.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.496
 At the end of your
four days, you'll

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:47.033
return to present your tabars
to a panel of expert judges.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.467
And after they've
tested them, they'll

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.369
declare one of you the
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.671
who walks out of here
with a check for 10 grand.

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:55.107
Do your best work, and
we'll see you in four days.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.543
Good luck, gentlemen.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.577
 Good luck, buddy.

00:03:00.312 --> 00:03:02.414
 Jarrod, Jimmy, welcome
back to the Forge.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:05.384
You guys have had four days
to work on your tabars.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.652
Jarrod, how'd it go for you?

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:10.590 line:0%
 Easy, smooth, worked
out how I wanted.

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.425 line:0%
I did a one-piece
construction head

00:03:12.491 --> 00:03:15.227 line:7%
out of some 5160 spring steel.

00:03:15.327 --> 00:03:18.364 line:0%
The handle is schedule
80 oil field pipe.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:21.400 line:0%
Dagger blade's made
out of schedule 160.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:26.272 line:0%
 All right, Jimmy, tell
the judges about your blade.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:29.808 line:0%
 The head's made out of
drive axle out of my truck.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:33.980 line:0%
Bottom was made out of the
trailer hinge ball off of it.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.314 line:0%
And I decided, since
we were doing all

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:36.783 line:0%
that, I'd go ahead and
make the dagger out

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.218 line:7%
of a piece of spring out of it.

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:40.887
 Gentlemen, now it's time to
figure out which one of you

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.221
in our "Forged in
Fire" champion.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.290
The judges will put your
blades through a series

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:45.591
of three tests.

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.159
There will be a strength
test, a sharpness test.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.527
And up first--

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.997
Doug.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:54.733
Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.336
Your tabars and hidden
daggers look beautiful,

00:03:57.436 --> 00:03:59.571
but it's time to find
out how lethal they are.

00:03:59.671 --> 00:04:01.174
To find that out, I
will take your weapon

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.776
and deliver some lethal
blows to this big carcass.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:04.377
Jarrod, you're up first.

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.177
You ready for this?

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:06.145
 Oh, I'm ready.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.146
 All right, let's do this.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.349
[rock music]

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:36.875
 Messed it up, dude.

00:04:36.975 --> 00:04:37.943
 That was awesome.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.478
You killed it.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.214
 All right, Jarrod, your
axe head here is very sharp.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:44.817
It really digs
into this carcass.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:48.087
The dagger, it felt good to
use it as a punch dagger.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:50.023
It penetrated deeply.

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:53.325
Overall, sir, your
weapon will kill.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:54.560
 [bleep] yeah, it'll kill.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:55.628
This is awesome!

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.996
 All right, Jimmy,
your turn, sir.

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:57.830
Are you ready?

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:58.564
 Let her rip.

00:04:58.665 --> 00:04:59.698
 Let's do this.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:02.302
[rock music]

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:31.931
 Oh, my god.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:34.433
 All right, Jimmy, let's
talk about your tabar here.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.767
Your axe head is sharp.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:38.137
It penetrated very
deep into this carcass.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:41.640
Now, your dagger, it feels good
in the hand as a punch dagger.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.477
More importantly, it will kill.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:52.184
 Bladesmiths, welcome to the
strength test-- the armored

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.120
warrior stab and chop.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:55.487
Remember, this test
is all about what

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:58.057
happens to your tabar
and your hidden dagger

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.658
and not what happens
to the warrior.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.159
Jarrod, you're up first.
You ready?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:01.893
 Get her done.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.630
[rock music]

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:25.518
 Well, Jarrod, you made
a nice-looking axe here.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:29.087
There's one little chip right
here, but the rest of it

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:30.556
is still pretty sharp.

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:31.923
All in all, I think
you did a great job.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.158
 Thanks, sir.

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:34.059
 All right, Jimmy,
you're up next.

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:35.093
You ready for this?

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:35.828
 I was.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:36.629
 [laughs]

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.032
[rock music]

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:57.917
 [exhales]

00:06:59.419 --> 00:07:01.921
 Well, Jimmy, your edge
held up really well here.

00:07:01.988 --> 00:07:03.756
There's no rolls or chips.

00:07:03.822 --> 00:07:07.560
But there was one swing where
the axe twisted in my hand,

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.528
and I think that's
to do with the fact

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:12.431
that the oval
handle here is just

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:13.632
out of alignment with the head.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:16.001
It's about five degrees off.

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:19.204
But in all, your axe held up
well in the strength test.

00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:19.972
Nice job.

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:26.912
 All right,
bladesmiths, this is

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.547
the sharpness test--
the sugar cane

00:07:28.613 --> 00:07:32.751
chop and the leather vest stab.

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.219
Jarrod, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:34.286 --> 00:07:34.853
 Yes, sir.

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:35.721
 Let's do this.

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.590
[rock music]

00:07:58.577 --> 00:08:01.646
All right, Jarrod,
your edge is sharp.

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:04.116
Also, in stabbing,
it punctured all

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:06.419
the way through, not an issue.

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:11.157
Overall, sir, the edge
of your weapons will cut.

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:12.191
All right, Jimmy,
your turn, sir.

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:13.159
You ready?

00:08:13.226 --> 00:08:13.892
 Let's do it.

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:15.861
 Let's do this.

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.830
[rock music]

00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:42.721
All right, Jimmy.

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.890
The one thing I noticed is
the way this is wrapped.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:48.060
It's twisted a little bit,
and it rotates in my hand.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:49.828
But it's sharp.

00:08:49.895 --> 00:08:53.132
Also, your dagger
here does puncture.

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:57.069
And overall, it will cut.

00:08:57.135 --> 00:09:00.673
 Jarrod, Jimmy, our new
"Forged in Fire" champion is--

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:04.209
Jarrod.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:05.411
Congratulations.

00:09:05.477 --> 00:09:06.612
You're the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:09.848
Jimmy, please
surrender your blade.

00:09:09.948 --> 00:09:11.450
JIMMY: It's kind of bittersweet.

00:09:11.517 --> 00:09:13.118
Jarrod, I'm glad for him.

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:14.787
But at the same time, you
know, it would've been

00:09:14.853 --> 00:09:17.089
nice to bring home the victory.

00:09:17.156 --> 00:09:17.923
It was challenging.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:18.591
Good job.

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:20.092
I'm proud of you.

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:21.660
 And it's real pressure.

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:22.994
But I had a blast here.

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:27.766
This was a great time,
just the whole experience.

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.802
 Jarrod, you are the new
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:32.338
And that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:32.404 --> 00:09:33.205
Good job, brother.

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:34.674
[applause]

00:09:35.607 --> 00:09:38.109
How are you feeling right now?

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.344
 Feels great.

00:09:39.445 --> 00:09:40.946
 Hey, man, a man
of thousand words.

00:09:41.012 --> 00:09:43.682
Please present your
weapon to the judges.

00:09:43.748 --> 00:09:46.218
 I just won "Forged in Fire."

00:09:46.285 --> 00:09:49.387
Yeah, I'm pretty excited.

00:09:49.454 --> 00:09:50.755
Planning on buying a house--

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:52.724
[laughs] as soon
as I find a house,

00:09:52.824 --> 00:09:54.693
and I can buy it with $10,000.

00:09:54.759 --> 00:09:56.528
Probably not, but-- [chuckles]

00:09:56.595 --> 00:10:00.199
[rock music]

